1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,248
A new Solana token shows hundreds of early
buyers. It looks like organic demand.

2
00:00:05,548 --> 00:00:11,531
But often it is one actor. One wallet
funds dozens of fresh addresses, they all

3
00:00:11,531 --> 00:00:15,393
buy in the first seconds, and later sell
to retail.

4
00:00:15,693 --> 00:00:20,437
Trackers show you who bought. They almost
never show who stands behind them. Unmask

5
00:00:20,437 --> 00:00:21,637
answers exactly that.

6
00:00:21,937 --> 00:00:26,813
The whole interface is a Telegram bot.
Type slash, and the commands appear.

7
00:00:27,113 --> 00:00:28,971
Check, then a token address.

8
00:00:29,271 --> 00:00:34,708
Risk seventy-two out of a hundred. High
concentration. Two clusters. The first one

9
00:00:34,708 --> 00:00:40,012
is six wallets that received ninety-two
percent of everything the analysed early

10
00:00:40,012 --> 00:00:40,742
buyers got.

11
00:00:41,042 --> 00:00:46,550
Here is the graph the bot sends with it.
Each circle is a cluster. The grey dots

12
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:51,645
are wallets outside the cluster that
connect to it. Here, a common funder.

13
00:00:51,645 --> 00:00:54,881
Thick red lines: one funder paying many
buyers.

14
00:00:55,181 --> 00:00:59,737
The diamonds are a single piece of
evidence tying a group of addresses

15
00:00:59,737 --> 00:01:03,447
together. They are not transfers between
those addresses.

16
00:01:03,747 --> 00:01:07,880
Another token. Three clusters, and one
funder feeding all three.

17
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:11,988
Look at the red fan spreading out of a
single grey wallet.

18
00:01:12,288 --> 00:01:17,415
And for contrast, a clean token. Risk
zero. No related groups found. Unmask does

19
00:01:17,415 --> 00:01:18,697
not invent clusters.

20
00:01:18,997 --> 00:01:24,620
A token it has not seen takes about two
minutes, with progress messages. After

21
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:26,567
that, the result is cached.

22
00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:29,978
Every claim comes with evidence. Tap
Evidence.

23
00:01:30,278 --> 00:01:35,322
For each cluster you get the type. Shared
funder, identical amounts, the same slot,

24
00:01:35,322 --> 00:01:39,880
an indirect link. Which wallets are
involved. And the time window, in block

25
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,913
time or in slots.

26
00:01:41,213 --> 00:01:46,721
The same data is in the public API.
Clusters, confidence, supply share, and

27
00:01:46,721 --> 00:01:50,687
the full evidence list. Anyone can replay
it on chain.

28
00:01:50,987 --> 00:01:56,084
And if the data is incomplete, Unmask says
so. It never shows incomplete data as

29
00:01:56,084 --> 00:01:56,467
clean.

30
00:01:56,767 --> 00:02:02,291
How it works. We take the first buyers of
a token and pull each wallet's funding

31
00:02:02,291 --> 00:02:07,332
history through an RPC pool. RPC Fast
serves the recent history, archival

32
00:02:07,332 --> 00:02:09,956
providers back it up for older tokens.

33
00:02:10,256 --> 00:02:14,578
We build a funding graph and prune the
hubs. Exchanges, routers, program

34
00:02:14,578 --> 00:02:17,640
accounts. Otherwise everything glues into
one blob.

35
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:23,520
Wallets sharing a funder inside a narrow
time window get merged. Indirect links are

36
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:28,764
added. Behavioural signals, like identical
amounts in the same slot, raise the

37
00:02:28,764 --> 00:02:29,503
confidence.

38
00:02:29,803 --> 00:02:35,140
This is a signal about financial links. It
is not proof of insider trading, and not

39
00:02:35,140 --> 00:02:38,162
financial advice. The limits are in the
README.

40
00:02:38,462 --> 00:02:43,614
What is next. Deeper buyer samples on
faster RPC, and monitoring of new

41
00:02:43,614 --> 00:02:44,267
launches.

42
00:02:44,567 --> 00:02:47,586
Unmask. See who is behind the buyers.

